# Vue Frontend Rules

## Tooling & Commands

- Use Node 20.19+ (per `package.json` engines). Install dependencies with `npm install`.
- Dev server: `npm run dev` (default port 5173). Build: `npm run build`. Preview: `npm run preview`.
- Keep the TypeScript config strict; do not disable `noImplicitAny` or `strictNullChecks`.
- Prefer `<script setup lang="ts">` syntax for components.

## Architecture & State

- Organize feature views under `src/views/**`, reusable components under `src/components/**`, and composables under `src/composables/**`.
- Use Pinia stores (`src/stores/**`) for cross-view state; avoid prop drilling when a store fits better.
- Keep routing definitions in `src/router/index.ts`; lazy-load route components for large views.
- Centralize API calls in dedicated modules (e.g., `src/api/**`); define response/request types that mirror the FastAPI schemas.

## Styling & UX

- Global styles live in `src/assets/main.css`; feature-specific styles should be scoped within components.
- Follow accessible color contrast; prefer semantic HTML + ARIA where needed.
- Use icons in `src/components/icons/**` for consistency; avoid ad-hoc SVG duplication.

## Testing & Quality

- Unit/component tests: add Vitest specs under `src` mirrored next to the file or inside `tests/unit`.
- Use Vue Test Utils together with Vitest for interactive components.
- Run `npm run type-check` and `npm run build` before submitting PRs; fix lint/type warnings proactively.

## Backend Integration

- Base API URL should come from `import.meta.env.VITE_API_BASE_URL`; default to `http://localhost:8000`.
- Handle fetch errors centrally (e.g., composables or API layer) and surface helpful UI messages.
- Update generated/handwritten TS types whenever backend schemas change; keep the change in the same PR.
